                            <comment id="14516803" author="yzhdanov" created="Tue, 28 Apr 2015 10:50:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;does not fit&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14611944" author="dmagda" created="Thu, 2 Jul 2015 13:19:47 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Also was reproduced with&lt;br/&gt;
IgniteCacheClientQueryReplicatedNodeRestartSelfTest.testRestarts&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14613200" author="dmagda" created="Fri, 3 Jul 2015 13:47:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Reproduced on&lt;br/&gt;
GridCacheClientNodePortableMetadataMultinodeTest.testFailoverOnStart for IgniteGridGain configuration&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14618154" author="dmagda" created="Wed, 8 Jul 2015 07:43:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged to the master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14638431" author="dmagda" created="Thu, 23 Jul 2015 08:06:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The assertion arose because sometimes a node, that was joining a topology, sent to its previous node order equal to 0. That previous node considered this as an error, however this node had &quot;node add finished message&quot; for that joining node that had to be sent to it. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now if a node receives 0 as an order from its next node it checks its pending messages queue before failing the next node.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reviewed by Yakov, merged to the main development branch.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
